# P3 enrollment and campaign-boundary preparation

Read-only preparation only. No production source was edited or executed. Inputs were the accepted P3 plan/spec, the principal native-prefix notes, unchanged `operations.py`/`cli.py`, focused immutable repository APIs, and the P1 frozen preimage at `admission-p2/principal-preimages/campaign_admission.py` (SHA-256 `7e15ed500121b4c85df7a838feab51750e1f476a3e5427b9d1a0b1f0f58a89d9`). I did not read the moving live admission/runtime/provider sources. The inspected unchanged source hashes were `operations.py` `8164379a88d045c795ce3487683c5d5d911e56583d0555a01551e934cdea2bcc` and `cli.py` `59044289f6f8cd3050e5f3604c30813f7f627fd221651af6ea76c74b4a6feb22`.

## Public plumbing and compatibility

- Extend `_run_campaign_v5` with `campaign_policy_ref: ArtifactRefV5 | None = None`. Existing `**kwargs` production/development wrappers keep forwarding it.
- Extend `render_production_command_v5` with the same optional argument and default. Preserve all existing return keys and launch/summary schemas; enrollment is pinned in rendered `argv`/PowerShell command.
- For `run-campaign` and `resume-campaign`, add the exact optional pair `--campaign-policy-path` and `--campaign-policy-sha256`. Both absent means `None`; exactly one present is an invalid request; both present are passed through `ArtifactRefV5` so the existing closed path/digest grammar applies. Do not add these options to prepare or single-round commands.
- Dispatch passes the parsed optional reference to the selected campaign operation. An omitted pair remains the exact legacy default. A supplied pair is an expectation, never an authority substitute.
- A fresh enrolled `run-campaign` rendering includes the explicit prepared policy ref. Every enrolled pending-response `resume_command` includes the binding's independently authenticated `policy_ref`, even when the current resume invocation omitted the pair. A legacy resume renders no policy flags.
- Do not change `CampaignLaunchV5` or `CampaignRoundLaunchV5` fields, defaults, canonical bytes, keys, or identity formulas. Fresh launch remains the same `CampaignLaunchV5(authenticated.manifest_ref, adapter_config_ref, token, started_epoch_ms)` under key `manifest.sha256`. Round configuration/start values remain unchanged.

## Enrollment state machine inside the launch lock

All selection, authentication, freshness, enrollment, and launch publication remain inside the existing `adapter_state_transition(namespace="campaign-launch", key=manifest.sha256)` lock. Adapter composition/validation remains the first read-only host-identity check.

1. Discover campaign launch and admission state without implicit typed-state repair. Authenticate supplied policy bytes before constructing any binding. Require exact equality to the invocation's original `authenticated.manifest_ref`, `adapter_config_ref`, owner digest, and repository-root identity, in addition to the frozen P1 prepared-policy checks.
2. Existing launch plus `resume=False` keeps the current “use resume-campaign” failure. Existing launch plus `resume=True` authenticates the original launch tuple first, then discovers enrollment even when `campaign_policy_ref` is omitted. If supplied, it must equal the enrolled binding ref. No binding plus omitted ref is legacy. No binding plus supplied ref fails; never enroll an already launched legacy campaign.
3. No launch plus `resume=True` keeps the current “use run-campaign” failure. It must not turn a binding-only interrupted publication into a resume operation.
4. No launch plus omitted ref takes the unchanged legacy fresh-launch path. It must not accept an existing binding: a binding-only state requires the same explicit policy pin to continue.
5. No launch plus explicit ref is the only enrollment path. Before the first possible write, authenticate the expected binding identities and a real fresh/no-start/no-spend census: no contradictory launch half, no round configuration or round-start state for this campaign, no round journal, no checkpoint/committed record, no request or invocation, no reservation/response/terminal/charged usage, and no resource/candidate state indicating a begun round. Retain the existing local graph/ledger verification as an additional check; do not use it instead of the focused immutable census.
6. With freshness proved, publish or authenticate exactly `CampaignAdmissionBindingV5(5, explicit_policy_ref, authenticated.manifest_ref, adapter_config_ref, token, repository.root_identity_sha256)` under namespace `campaign-admission`, key `manifest.sha256`. Then append the unchanged campaign launch. Never overwrite either value.

The explicit crash cases are closed as follows:

- Both binding halves absent: create the exact binding, then launch.
- Exact binding value and index present, launch absent: accept only the same explicit policy after repeating all identity and freshness checks, then append launch.
- Exact binding value present with only its authority index missing: after the same checks and before launch, call `recover_typed_state_index` with the exact expected binding. This helper may publish only the missing index. Re-read admission with `repair=False` and require exact equality before launch.
- Authority without value, changed/noncanonical value, different policy/binding, foreign key, malformed namespace member, contradictory/orphan launch, or any start/spend evidence: fail closed with no write.

Do not catch a broad authentication failure and call recovery. Recovery is permitted only for the independently identified sole missing binding-index case. In particular, all policy/config/manifest/root/owner and freshness reads must complete before recovery. P1 admission discovery remains immutable and is not changed to repair implicitly.

## Facts required from reviewed P2

P3 must consume P2's reviewed data-only immutable facts; it must not recreate ledger arithmetic, filter the repository, call whole completed-history authentication on a partial campaign, or infer a round from request content. Exact names/signatures are intentionally deferred to the P2 review. P3 needs the reviewed facts/composition to provide:

- authenticated original manifest/config/owner/root and campaign launch/deadline identities;
- a union census of campaign-round configuration and campaign-round-started value/index members, with canonical keys, exact pair agreement, and rejection of malformed, orphan, foreign, conflicting, gapped, or out-of-range state;
- all observed started round indices, whether each is settled, and whether successful cleanup exists, so no target success can hide a later pending/failed started round;
- a prefix view for the candidate round that excludes an existing unstarted candidate from prior attempted/spend counters and preserves the original admission for an already started continuation;
- exact `evaluated_feedback_rounds`, `attempted_rounds`, `external_attempts`, `total_tokens`, and finite `Decimal cost_usd` for `campaign_boundary_decision_v5`;
- evaluated count as distinct round indices having an authenticated committed `status == "evaluated"` record with campaign evidence, intersected with actual successful-cleanup indices;
- authenticated request/invocation/ledger usage and settlement facts, including all real prior packages and earlier roles in an active round, without a fake current package;
- explicit contradiction/failure state rather than a permissive partial result.

The enrollment freshness use needs the same immutable census specialized to zero launch/start/spend. If P2 does not expose enough to establish this without reconstructing its private rules, P3 must stop for a focused P2 interface extension and review; it must not guess the interface or copy its logic.

## Boundary placement and state transitions

Legacy (`admission is None`) follows the current loop byte-for-behavior: reconcile, reuse, deadline/provider checks, configuration/start publication, runtime, cleanup/failure handling, final verification and the existing `max_feedback_rounds` result.

For enrollment, reload/authenticate admission and settled facts at each decision; do not cache absence. Apply the pure P1 decision only at a settled boundary:

1. Reconcile existing paid roles for the current observed round first.
2. Authenticate ownership/integrity, journal/ledger/resource facts, terminal/committed state, and cleanup. Existing pending, runtime/provider, cleanup, authority, clock/deadline, and status/novelty failures keep their current return/break reason before policy stopping.
3. Before reporting target success, inspect the global observed-start census. Every observed started round must have been reconciled and settled with successful cleanup, and no later pending/failed/contradictory start may be hidden by an earlier reused round.
4. After every accepted settled round, reused or newly executed, recompute facts and the policy decision. This is required even on the final manifest round so reaching the target there reports `evaluated_feedback_target_reached` instead of falling through to `max_feedback_rounds`.
5. Before creating a missing next-round adapter config or `campaign-round` state, recompute the decision from the settled prior prefix. A non-`admit` result causes no config, state, request, or synthetic outcome write.
6. For an already existing configuration with no start, validate the unchanged configuration/owner shape, recheck existing deadline/provider precedence, then recompute from the prior prefix immediately before appending `campaign-round-started`. A non-`admit` result leaves the pre-start configuration observed and performs no further write.
7. For an already started current round, do not rerun new-round admission using current-round spend. Continue only under its authenticated original start/admission and persisted campaign/round deadlines; P2 request/ledger guards own per-call continuation.

The boundary call receives the reviewed facts verbatim:

```python
decision = campaign_boundary_decision_v5(
    policy=admission.policy,
    manifest=manifest,
    evaluated_feedback_rounds=facts.evaluated_feedback_rounds,
    attempted_rounds=facts.attempted_rounds,
    external_attempts=facts.external_attempts,
    total_tokens=facts.total_tokens,
    cost_usd=facts.cost_usd,
)
```

`evaluated_feedback_target_reached` returns outer `status="completed"` with that distinct reason. `insufficient_milestone_reserve` returns `status="stopped"`. Neither appends a round outcome, cleanup, finalizer, denial package, request, or other evidence. Existing summaries and count formulas are untouched. Existing failure-class exit-code behavior remains unchanged; the two policy reasons are successful operational exits unless the current CLI contract is independently ruled otherwise.

## Implementation/review checks for the follow-up

- Save fresh source preimages before the one-writer P3 edit; the hashes above are preparation observations, not authorization to overwrite changed source.
- Source/AST inspection must show: one optional operation argument and one optional renderer argument; exact CLI pair validation; enrollment append before unchanged launch append under the same lock; no implicit repair before freshness; only exact binding-index recovery; checks before config creation and before first start; checks after both reused and new settlements; and enrolled resume rendering pinned to the selected policy.
- Diff inspection must show no changes to old dataclasses, summary formulas, single-round commands, runtime/provider/cleanup logic, or legacy defaults. Scoped Ruff and in-memory compile are deferred to the authorized P3 implementation/review; no tests, imports, synthetic artifacts, readers, summaries, provider calls, or execution belong to this preparation.

No architectural ruling is requested. The only implementation dependency is the reviewed P2 facts surface described above.

## Frozen P2 interface refresh

This addendum supersedes the preceding suggestion that a missing composed boundary interface would require a separate P2 task. The inspected P2 review freeze is `admission-p2/review-freeze-01/campaign_admission.py`, SHA-256 `07fdea2f5aa8d86b58a1f7537306253dc63fcb8ed6ed2290ddf745ad643e5d14`. P2 is still under independent review; these are preparation mappings, not approval of that source.

The concrete reusable private surface is:

- `_state_names_v5(repository, namespace) -> tuple[str, ...]`: immutable value/index union census with closed key grammar.
- `_selected_campaign_launch_v5(*, repository, manifest, admission) -> CampaignLaunchV5`: global selected-launch census, `repair=False`, foreign-key rejection, and exactly-one requirement. Its exactly-one wrapper is for launched execution; P3 freshness needs a narrow zero-or-one census extracted from the same selection logic rather than duplicating it.
- `_selected_round_states_v5(*, repository, manifest, admission, namespace) -> dict[int, CampaignRoundLaunchV5]`: global immutable selection for `campaign-round` and `campaign-round-started`, including foreign-key, duplicate, and out-of-range rejection. P3 can pass the in-memory expected admission before binding publication.
- `_require_round_config_matches_original_v5(original, current) -> None`: preserves all non-derived original configuration identities.
- `_load_campaign_round_authority_v5(*, repository, manifest, admission, round_index, owner_token_sha256) -> _LiveCampaignRoundAuthorityV5`: exact launched/started prefix, original config/owner/root, and stored deadline authentication. It remains the already-started live path and cannot represent a pre-start boundary.
- `_campaign_event_rounds_v5(repository, manifest) -> tuple[int, ...]`: canonical global round-journal directory census.
- `_role_packages_v5(*, repository, manifest, round_index, payloads, policy)`: exact role-call/journal binding, primary-position prefix, and envelope authentication.
- `_load_live_role_prefix_v5(*, repository, manifest, authority, request, round_index) -> _LiveRolePrefixV5`: reviewed request-specific prior prefix. It returns prior evaluated/attempted/receipt counters plus replay, but deliberately requires an actual started current round and real request. P3 must not call it with a synthetic request or reinterpret its `attempted_rounds=round_index - 1` result as a post-settlement boundary.

The concrete architecture gap is limited: no frozen P2 composition represents (a) enrollment freshness before any launch, (b) an existing configuration before first start, or (c) counters after a newly/reused settled round, including a whole-campaign observed-start check. P3 may add focused data-only freshness/boundary facts in `campaign_admission.py` under P3 review. That composition must reuse the selectors/package/resource/ledger proof already used by P2, keep `_load_campaign_round_authority_v5`, `_load_live_role_prefix_v5`, and `require_live_role_admission_v5` behavior unchanged, and avoid copied ledger arithmetic.

Freshness is scoped to selected operational authority for this manifest: launch/round/start state, journals, requests/invocations, ledger reservations/terminals/charged usage, and begun resource/candidate authority must be absent. Authenticated prepared-policy, source, fixed-parent, manifest/config, and other required evidence artifacts are legitimate and must not be rejected merely because the repository is not byte-empty. Legacy launch loading retains its existing operational repair behavior and order; only new enrolled selection/freshness uses immutable reads before its explicitly gated binding-index recovery.
